  "articleBody": "Thinking about new baseboards? Great choice, they really make a room pop! But before you jump in, there are a few things you should consider to make sure it goes smoothly. First, think about the current state of your walls and floors. If they're uneven, it's going to make getting a clean, tight fit a real challenge. A professional can assess this and prepare properly. Second, consider the style of baseboard you want. Are you trying to match existing trim in other rooms, or are you going for a whole new look? This impacts the type of material and profile you'll choose. Third, who's handling the finishing touches? Will your installer fill nail holes and caulk the joints, or is that something you'll need to coordinate separately before painting? Getting clear on this upfront avoids surprises. Finally, think about the timing. Baseboards usually go in after your drywall is done but before the final paint job. This sequencing allows for proper prep and a clean finish. For long runs, lots of corners, or if you're aiming for a high-end painted finish, having an experienced team like HH Remodeling LLC handle it can save you a lot of hassle and ensure a beautiful result.",
